Fizzbuzz returned to his main stash to prepare for the final part of
his journey. He busied himself with mundane tasks, such as enchanting
armour and calculating how many charges he had left on his collection
of wands. After he was finished with each item he tidely put it into
the bag sitting on the floor, in order to keep his workplace tidy. No
Rogue can be successful if they aren't organised.

Looking through his inventory, he noticed a pair of wands of
cancellation. Realising that these could have a catastrophic effect if
mixed with his magical sacks, he decided that it was necessary to keep
them in a slightly safer place. Rummaging around in his stash, he found
an tattered old sack which he deemed suitable for storing them in. He
also threw in some holy water and scrolls of remove-curse - everything
he would need in an emergency.

As a matter of procedure he grabbed a can of grease from his stash, and
vigourously applied it to the sack. "Right," he thinks to himself,
"That's a job well done," as he goes to put the grease away.

"You put the sack in the bag of holding. You are blasted by a magical
explosion."

In a clumsy mistake, he had put the sack containing the wands of
cancellation into his bag of holding instead of the grease. He'd lost
everything.

Well, not quite everything. He still had his armour and his weapons,
his magical rings, his collection of rare cockatrice eggs, and a few
other assorted items which he had still in his main inventory. Most
importantly he also still had theBell of Opening, and Candelabrum of
Invocation which he knew were necessary for
his adventure. He also had the Master Key of Thievery, another greatly
helpful item.

In fact, when he came to think about it, Fizzbuzz realised that all
he'd really lost were his collection of wands, potions of healing, and
amulets of life-saving. In fact none of these were really necessary for
him to continue... sure, they would be helpful (especially the wands of
death and teleport), but not vital. And he wasn't planning on using the
Life Saving Amulets anyway.

Fizzbuzz settled down to try to replace some of these items, by a spot
of "Pudding Farming". After a while however, he realised that it wasn't
helping much (although he did gain a little Holy water and some potions
of healing) and so he decided to carry on anyway. Without any further
ado, he retrieved the amulet and ascended to the status of Demigod.

Notes:

Magicmapping and conflict made the plane of air much easier than
expected. Thisis where I thought I'd have the most difficulty, but not
going through the clouds (magic mapping showed a route through) and
using conflict prevented the Air Elementals from hitting me once.

Kos was the ultimate God of crappy artifacts (Werebane, Dragonbane,
Orcrist, Ogrewhatever etc...). Eventually I got fed up and decided to
enchant my silver sabres and give them cool names instead. I later got
Magicbane (bones pile), Frostbrand and Stormbringer (crowning).

I was worried about having no /oD for Rodney, but 'Trice Eggs did a
fine job instead.

This was wishless genocideless, but not really out of choice. By the
time I'd found the Castle wand and identified the scroll, I felt strong
enough to do without them. Besides, I blew them up in the bag of
holding...

The Riders were much easier than expected. They fell from 3 dagger
throws. I was only hit by Death once when I only threw one dagger on my
first turn, and he reduced my HP from 401 to 385.

I came across a few bones files, but none were really helpful. Well
actually, one contained the GDSM, but that was in a shop and I couldn't
get to the loot until I'd killed the shopkeeper (by which time I would
have been able to get my own GDSM anyway).



